------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the MIT License above covers
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

It covers AgroDesign Studios' own code in this folder: every file not named
below, including the files the app shares with AgroDesign's own applications
(under frontend/src/ and frontend/vite-plugins/), which are published here
under the same licence.

It does not cover, and does not change the licence of, the following. Each
keeps its own licence:

- frontend/public/vendor/pymol/3.2.0a-edcda80f-s3-pyodide-314.0.7/ — the
  in-browser PyMOL runtime: Pyodide 314.0.7 (Mozilla Public License 2.0),
  CPython (PSF License Agreement), Open-Source PyMOL 3.2.0a (its own licence),
  NumPy (BSD 3-Clause) and the code each of them bundles. The full texts are
  in that folder's licenses/ (LICENSE.*.txt, NOTICES.*.txt; where Pyodide's
  source is: SOURCE.pyodide.txt). The folder's README.md, host.js and
  worker.js are AgroDesign Studios' own and are covered by the MIT License.

- The patches to Open-Source PyMOL — patches/*.patch in that runtime folder
  and pymol-wasm/patches/*.patch (byte-identical copies) — follow the licence
  of the Open-Source PyMOL files they change.

  Patch 0011 (0011-mypng-failed-read-builds-no-image.patch) changes
  base64_decode in Open-Source PyMOL's layer0/MyPNG.cpp. PyMOL took that
  decoder and its decoding table from a Stack Overflow post, whose posts were
  published under CC BY-SA 3.0; licenses/NOTICES.pymol-third-party.txt
  (section "base64 decoding table") records the most likely source and
  licence. The patch is published as it is; the lines it changes keep that
  origin and licence.

- pymol-wasm/notices/*.LICENSE — licence texts of upstream code inside
  Open-Source PyMOL, kept verbatim (pymol-wasm/notices/README.md says from
  where).

- In pymol-wasm/tests/es300_rewrite_test.cpp (marked in the file),
  stringReplaceAll and call_compute_color_for_light are copied from
  Open-Source PyMOL's layer0/ShaderMgr.cpp, and old_es300 is patch 0005's
  code (a patch to Open-Source PyMOL, as above). Both follow Open-Source
  PyMOL's licence (Copyright (C) Schrodinger, LLC; full text in
  licenses/LICENSE.pymol.txt of the runtime folder above).

- In frontend/src/pages/pymol-viewer/pymolSettingsData.ts, the generated rows
  (GENERATED_SETTINGS) are Open-Source PyMOL's own setting help, taken from
  its data/setting_help.csv; in frontend/src/pages/pymol-viewer/
  pymolMenuData.ts, the generated menu (PYMOL_MENU) is Open-Source PyMOL's
  menu bar, its labels and commands, taken from its pymol/_gui.py. Both
  follow Open-Source PyMOL's licence (Copyright (C) Schrodinger, LLC; full
  text in licenses/LICENSE.pymol.txt of the runtime folder above). The rest of
  each file is AgroDesign Studios' own and is covered by the MIT License.

- The npm packages frontend/package-lock.json names (React, 3Dmol.js, Vite and
  the others). They are not in this folder; npm installs them, and each keeps
  its own licence. A built HTML file lists the ones it carries, with their
  texts, in its Help > Licences tab and in the repository's NOTICE.

- frontend/src/pages/structure-html-export/__fixtures__/1crn.cif — PDB entry
  1CRN from the wwPDB, whose data is free of copyright restrictions (CC0 1.0).

"PyMOL" is a trademark of Schrodinger, LLC.
